{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are","id":1403917,"title":"Do the Dragon-blooded truly delude themselves the Solars and Lunars are","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-21T18:19:40-07:00","id":1403917,"title":"Do the Dragon-blooded truly delude themselves the Solars and Lunars are","content":"&quot;Anathema&quot;, devil-possessed humans? Or do they know the Solars and Lunars are Exalted, but consider they are threats to their supremacy, so must be hunted down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T18:53:46-07:00","id":1403921,"title":"","content":"The Immaculate Texts identify them as Exalted, but also as being doomed to madness because humans aren't meant to wield the power of the sun and moon. You'll notice that this isn't <i>exactly</i> inaccurate; the Celestials do have a historical tendency to lose their shit.<br /> <br /> Whether individual DBs know this depends on how versed they are in the particulars of the faith and Texts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T18:56:59-07:00","id":1403922,"title":"","content":"In 3rd Edition, the higher ranks of the Immaculate Order, and those considered enlighted enough by the Order to be told, know that Solars and Lunars are Exalted. The idea that they're people possessed by demons who are unsaveable is a simplified version that they tell the masses to avoid confusing them. However, those who know this still believe the Solars and Lunars are Anathema, because &quot;Anathema&quot; doesn't mean &quot;demon who possessed a human and glows gold or silver&quot;, it means &quot;a person fundamentally opposed to the Immaculate Order's view of the Perfected Hierarchy, the proper order of the the universe&quot;. Solars and Lunars are Anathema by default, but others can be declared Anathema as well, depending on their nature and behavior - some Exigents, for example, are considered Anathema, but others aren't, if they're willing to support the Dragon-Bloods' social order. And Sidereals mostly aren't, though some Sidereals are trying to now tweak the scriptures to say that &quot;beings with star motifs and Fate powers are Anathema if they support known Anathema like Solars&quot;, to get the Gold Faction Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Immaculate Order knows that Solars and Lunars are Exalted. Their position is that that doesn't matter - the power of the Sun and Moon are too great, and inevitably drives the holders to madness and destruction, so they still need to be put down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T18:57:16-07:00","id":1403923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are#post1403917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Anathema&quot;, devil-possessed humans? Or do they know the Solars and Lunars are Exalted, but consider they are threats to their supremacy, so must be hunted down?</div> </div> </div> </div>The new Dragon-Blooded books discuss this. Basically lay folk are given the Anathema story because it's convenient. Immaculate monks know that Anathema aren't <i>actually</i> possessed by demons, but they're both powerful in a way that endangers people <i>and</i> present a threat to Dragon-Blooded rulership with every day they continue to draw breath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-21-2020, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T20:28:44-07:00","id":1403935,"title":"","content":"Its also hardly &quot;deluding themselves&quot; when that's what they're taught. The majority are taught that demons stole the power of the sun and moon and occasionally possess people to do bad things considering the tendency for Solars and Lunars to do things that cause problems for most Dragonblood run societies ,even discounting collateral damage from not wanting to die to a Wyld Hunt, this tends to check out. Eventually the more studious and loyal will get it explained that yes Solars and Lunars are exalts, but well the influences get thrust onto random people and don't mesh well with the human psyche after a long time and the results will get ugly even if the power didn't end up in the wrong hands off the bat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T20:43:45-07:00","id":1403937,"title":"","content":"A fun thing to consider: because Dragon-Blooded Exaltations tend to occur before Celestial Exaltations do, and since they\u2019re mutually exclusive, anyone who Exalts as a Solar or Lunar by definition was passed over by the Dragons. The Sun and the Moon only choose mortals unsuited to leadership, making their wondrous powers of leadership a terrible curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T21:26:04-07:00","id":1403938,"title":"","content":"I wrote an in-character spin on this topic, in the context of an NPC giving the Dragon-Blooded PCs a pep talk after becoming shikari:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Immaculate Abbot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the world when all was the formless Wyld, Gaia birthed the Elemental Dragons from shards of her own soul. They, in turn, built Creation by mixing the elements of Air, Wood, Fire, Water, and Earth. Once they completed their labors, Gaia bid the Dragons calm and spread to the corners of the world. And into that calmed world came Gaia's Grandchildren, the Terrestrial Exalted, the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> For a time, all was peaceful. But as the years passed the gods of the sun and moon and stars grew jealous of the Dragons' perfection. They consorted with demons, trading their virtue for sorcerous secrets. In a mockery of the Second Breath, they unleashed spirits to possess the innocent among humanity, marking them as Anathema to the Immaculate Order as dangerous to let run free as Wyld Fae or the restless dead. Luckily, the Dragon-Blooded were and are spared the corruption of Anathemetic possession - only a lesser human soul is susceptible.<br /> <br /> The ancestors of today's Dragon-Blooded pleaded with the gods to cage what they had wrought, but found no way to turn the sun and moon and stars from their path of dark emulation of the Dragon's grace. Instead, these Anathema subjugated the Dragon-Blooded with their strange ways and awesome powers. It was a dark time of tyranny and terror.<br /> <br /> Then, the Immaculate Dragons graced Creation in Exalted form to lead the fight of liberation. A great war was fought and the Anathema were brought low by the valiant sacrifice of upright soldiers. Their names and deeds are not for us to recall - for it is the Anathema who seek to mark the world with such force that they achieve immortality through fame and legend. The upright soldier puts family before self, nation before ambition, legion before fang, Dragons before gods, and Creation above all. Their names are the first of their many sacrifices for the righteous rule of the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> The Shogunate reigned in the Anathema's absence. Glorious Manses were erected. The land was healed from the sorcerous perversions of Cauldronists and demonic influence. The Dragon-Blooded host was fruitful and multiplied in Gaia's image. Art and culture reigned; it was a blessed time. But, it was not to last.<br /> <br /> A sickness swept across the world that killed nearly everything in its path. No type of creature was spared - even the plants withered and died from the Contagion's touch. Heaven closed its gates in fear. The Dragon-Blooded never abandoned the Blessed Isle, but the defenses at the furthest reaches of the Threshold were stranded without resupply or reinforcements. In that time of weakness, the Fair Folk amassed and breached the reality engines that once ringed Creation. Weakened by sickness, separated by swaths of fresh death, many legions fell to the mad assault. The inner sea was brimming with behemoths, and the nobles that rode them took turns corrupting the sea and lands beyond with whatever whims took their fancy.<br /> <br /> In that darkest hour, a young lieutenant led her Sworn Kinship into the Imperial Manse to find the trigger of the ancient Anathema weapon known as the Sword of Creation. Though none of her fellows survived the journey, the Scarlet Empress activated that most dangerous of devices, calling down lightning, coaxing forests to explode into splinters, rolling firestorms across the deserts, and summoning great waves to crash upon the shores. The Fae were slaughtered in as great of numbers as the Contagion took from the living. They were routed back beyond the edges of the world.<br /> <br /> Since that time seven hundred and sixty eight years ago we have prospered under the Scarlet Empress' enlightened rule. We have had peace to cultivate our souls, to seek understanding of the Dragons and their Immaculate visitation, and to climb the Perfected Hierarchy when we perish. The Scarlet Empress is like the Dragons in that she has transcended death so that she might see the Realm rule for all eternity. We faithful Immaculates keep the Five Diligent Practices and study the Five Noble Insights. Your decision to join the Wyld Hunt to ride down Anathema speaks to your strength of will; you will need every scrap of it against the trials to come.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T01:45:37-07:00","id":1403959,"title":"","content":"I still maintain that somewhere in the early Shogunate there would have been those who repeated propaganda that most demonized the Solar and Lunar Exalted so frequently that they really did come to believe it themselves. Or at least undermined their capacity to distinguish between truth and cynical opportunism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are?p=1403937#post1403937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fun thing to consider: because Dragon-Blooded Exaltations tend to occur before Celestial Exaltations do, and since they\u2019re mutually exclusive, anyone who Exalts as a Solar or Lunar by definition was passed over by the Dragons. The Sun and the Moon only choose mortals unsuited to leadership, making their wondrous powers of leadership a terrible curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it as a spurious argument that a Terrestrial might make, but I don't think it makes much sense as a thing to widely and deeply believe. They still know what the significance of their bloodlines is.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose that just requires a slight adjustment to the focus; it's not reaching adulthood without properly Exalting that signifies the lack of favour in the Perfected Hierarchy, it's having been born at all in a body other than one begat by the Dragon's Blood. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:28:16-07:00","id":1403989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are?p=1403959#post1403959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I suppose that just requires a slight adjustment to the focus; it's not reaching adulthood without properly Exalting that signifies the lack of favour in the Perfected Hierarchy, it's having been born at all in a body other than one begat by the Dragon's Blood. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. UnExalted Dynasts aren\u2019t disappointing because they did something to piss off the Dragons; they\u2019re disappointing because their failure to Exalt is proof that they were never as spiritually refined as their peers, due to past incarnations. It\u2019s often easy to retroactively find proof of a mortal Dynast\u2019s fundamental unworthiness (though they\u2019re still more refined than any other mortal). Some justifications cause more cognitive dissonance, but that\u2019s where faith comes in. The best and brightest mortal Dynasts will surely Exalt in future lives, if they can pass the spiritual tests of a life among the Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:49:24-07:00","id":1404003,"title":"","content":"I've said before today that the real falsehood of the immaculate order isn't that the solars and lunars are prone to madness and excess, but that the dragon blooded <i>aren't</i>. <br /> <br /> Given stewardship of Creation, the Dragon Blooded have run roughshod over the world, producing just as much individual suffering as the solars did. Yes, each individual is less powerful and less of a threat to creation as a whole, but dynasts alone outnumber the solars and lunars 14 to one. That adds up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T07:51:35-07:00","id":1404021,"title":"","content":"On a tangent, one of the cool things about originally portraying Anathema as believed by Dragon-Blooded to be reincarnating wicked sorcerers who had effectively broken the karmic wheel of reincarnation was how it interacted with Immaculate beliefs; these were originally mortals who'd done the ultimate bad thing and given up their place in the cycle of merit and development for stolen power and stolen eternal life, yet succumbed to the inevitable stresses from too much power for a mortal soul. It also kind of dovetailed a bit more with the mild critique of ideas of cycles of reincarnation as presenting possibilities for structural social inequity. There's a lot of motivation in it for Dragon-Blooded Dynasts who are keen to maintain their social structure. (Bonus for also fitting with Past Lives memories - it's possibly easier for Immaculate following Solars to believe they don't remember an ancient incarnation who made deals with the devil than thinking that they are a demon and none of their ancestors memories feel like that?).<br /> <br /> Being possessed by demons is fine of course (whenever edition that idea shifted happened!) just found it interesting to think about above given the recent conversations about Immaculate Order and the Realm etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:50:12-07:00","id":1404031,"title":"","content":"How the Dragon-Blooded think about the Sidereals? Do they revere them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:51:31-07:00","id":1404032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are?p=1403935#post1403935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its also hardly &quot;deluding themselves&quot; when that's what they're taught. The majority are taught that demons stole the power of the sun and moon and occasionally possess people to do bad things considering the tendency for Solars and Lunars to do things that cause problems for most Dragonblood run societies ,even discounting collateral damage from not wanting to die to a Wyld Hunt, this tends to check out. Eventually the more studious and loyal will get it explained that yes Solars and Lunars are exalts, but well the influences get thrust onto random people and don't mesh well with the human psyche after a long time and the results will get ugly even if the power didn't end up in the wrong hands off the bat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the learned could delude themselves the demons are capable of stealing powers from the Sun and Moon. And why they contrive to steal Celestial powers, when could simply bestow their own diabolical gifts to innocent humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 07-22-2020, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T09:54:00-07:00","id":1404042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are?p=1404031#post1404031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the Dragon-Blooded think about the Sidereals? Do they revere them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Dragon-Blooded are in the same position as the rest of Creation - they don't know the Sidereals exist. Again, the upper echelons of the Immaculate Order and Dynastic society in general are better-informed, though they probably still don't know <i>everything</i> about the Sidereals. The original writers of the Immaculate Texts, and Sidereal redactors over the centuries since then, have been careful to drop some hints about &quot;starry-eyed wise people&quot; being a thing that are around, and <i>aren't</i> automatically bad, so that if a Sidereal has to &quot;go loud&quot; during a Wyld Hunt or something, they have something to justify themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are?p=1404032#post1404032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the learned could delude themselves the demons are capable of stealing powers from the Sun and Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. Remember, nobody in the setting has our omniscient perspective, where we're told the &quot;true&quot; power of the Unconquered Sun, Luna, and other Incarnae. People could believe they're less overwhelmingly-incredible than they are. They certainly don't tend to <i>show off</i> that power, being busy with their &quot;retirement&quot; to the Jade Pleasure Dome, and haven't done much for millennia.<br /> <br /> Also, we actually <i>don't</i> know that it's impossible to steal power from the Sun or Moon. Supernatural beings and Exalts have pulled off thefts of power of that sort over the course of the history of the setting. We don't know if this will carry on into 3e, but in 2e, there was a mighty raksha lord, Laashe, who managed to trick the Unconquered Sun himself, and would have made himself into a power greater than the Sun if Luna hadn't managed to sneak up on him and trick him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why they contrive to steal Celestial powers, when could simply bestow their own diabolical gifts to innocent humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Immaculates are working on the assumption that the demons in question are trying to corrupt people and pull them away from the Perfected Hierarchy - not just the people they provide power to directly, but also others. Providing obviously demonic gifts wouldn't work for that: the average peasant, if she saw someone with horrible claws, fangs, burning with green alien fire, etc., isn't likely to worship or follow them, she's likely to run away. Whereas glowing with the light of the sun or moon, familiar celestial bodies, is familiar, comforting, even. And while the Solars and Lunars exercising their powers can be terrifying, they're also terrifying in a human way (or, sometimes in the Lunars' case, terrifying in a way that's familiar as a common animal). Thus, the Immaculate Philosophy claims, the demons trick more humans into following the Solars and Lunars, pulling them away from the Perfected Hierarchy, and corrupting even more souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T10:48:40-07:00","id":1404047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are?p=1404032#post1404032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the learned could delude themselves the demons are capable of stealing powers from the Sun and Moon. And why they contrive to steal Celestial powers, when could simply bestow their own diabolical gifts to innocent humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>First flaw in your hypothesis, &quot;learned people.&quot; Learned in what? The status of Solars, and Lunars as anathema is an Immaculate Order subject, they're the authority on the subject and they teach demons. So the majority of educations aren't gonna touch on the moon-mad and whatever the term for solar anathema are beyond potential signs of their presence again from the Order. If you wanted a non-Immaculate Order you'd have to go to Gods or the Anathema themselves. The Anathema whom your education says will probably end you as soon as talk to you and if they do talk to you have every reason to lie and try to subvert you meaning nothing they tell you can be trusted not counting the high likelyhood of getting executed for trying that since the risk of having been corrupted or replaced is so high. And Gods are probably gonna tow the Immaculate Order line on the terrestrial level because the order tends to be decent for some of the lower tier ones and if you aren't a considerable amount of power then openly teaching against the Order line will result in the Order going to deal with said God with considerable threat to the God's life,livelyhood, and power. <br /> <br /> So learned individuals are going to have learned this story because that's what was taught and then their education went a different way and well my sibling's doctorate in psychology does not exactly give them a brilliant understand on the history and specifics of architecture, agriculture, and naval warfare. Those seeking to know more are going to go back to the Order for more information who will ,eventually, tell them the bit about how the powers of the sun and moon were too much for human psyches and the bearers will eventually need to be put down to stop the horrors and its better to do so while they're fresh and weak before they've started trying to solve an overpopulation problem with flesh using the living as building materials. <br /> <br /> As for the second flaw, why steal the power of the sun and moon instead of using their own gifts? They do use their own gifts there are tons of warnings about interacting with demons because of the dangers they pose and while some of it is the boiler plate &quot;A blood ape wants little more in this world than to crack open your bones and drink the marrow&quot; others are of the dangers they pose to individuals in the gifts the offer. You want wealth, tools, luxury, and all the power those can bestow? This is the mark of the the Sigil's Dreamer talk with him and he'll tell you how many people you need to put that mark on to get your heart's desires. But why wouldn't demons steal power from the sun and moon if they could and use that to throw a wrench in things? Have you seen the mindset of demons Agata want to travel and carry people home, but they're also likely to drop them from half a mile up just to see how the former rider's splat makes the wasp feel; and Neomah make babies for people, but if you don't handle that properly your kid could end up half snake because the scale pattern on that one complimented the mother's eyes; The Hammer of the Forge of Night wants to make top quality items and equipment and for people to know their place, and she would very much appreciate it if you would give yourself to her because she thinks you would make a marvelous set of cuff links. So the idea that there were demons that wanted to upset the Hierarchy of how the world works and decided the best way to do that would be steal the power of the sun and moon and use that as a lure to the unfaithful to gain possession of the person and use them to cause more chaos, havoc, and upset the Hierarchy is not a hard sell.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine the existence of black market exigence, and dirty bomb exigents are also contributors to the logic that such things might be done.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T10:59:35-07:00","id":1404048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are?p=1404031#post1404031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the Dragon-Blooded think about the Sidereals? Do they revere them?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't think on Sidereals most of the time. The 3e books ont he topic note that Sidereals basically are hidden agents of Heaven. The stuff about them in general in the exoteric stuff most folks get is that wise people come up now and again and give the Dragon-Blooded advice. Those in the know about htem usually see them as agents of Heaven who give input in the needs of Desitny, tend to give good advice, and like the Dragon-Blooded are spiritually enlightened enough to handle this stuff. &quot;Hidden equals&quot; is kind of the gist I think the Sidereals want to present themselves as in context of the Philosophy, but again, most folks don't even know who they are, and there are some who do know about htem who don't trust them but see them as anicllary to the Philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:04:55-07:00","id":1404049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are?p=1404032#post1404032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the learned could delude themselves the demons are capable of stealing powers from the Sun and Moon. And why they contrive to steal Celestial powers, when could simply bestow their own diabolical gifts to innocent humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>As others stated, &quot;learned&quot; is something that you have to define here, as you beg the question that this means they would know the capaiblities of the Sun, Moon, and the demons that supposedly made the Anatheam. And even then, folks who get deep into the theology know that isn't hte case. It's kind of like any religious studies sutff. Most people don't know about htings like the Nicean Creed, or that what angels and devils look like in modern depictions is influenced by Daunte's fan ficiton. And there's a difference between the concept of karma that is often talked about by folks in the general US public and even to some extent I find with folks from Buddhist and Hindu-majority countires, and what like, serious practiioners in those faiths actually describe it as.<br /> <br /> There's a big dfiference between what the lay members of a society know and describe things and what folks who actually take the time to research do. Most scholars probably do learn the dmeon thing is just shorthand to describe the inehritence fo Exaltation and that the actual origins are foggy at best. Kind of like how a lot of folks eventaully if they dig into it learn that no, the Bible doesn't describe anything about layers of Hell, and angels were effing weird with too many eyeballs a lot of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:10:03-07:00","id":1404051,"title":"","content":"It's not necessarily &quot;deluded&quot; because most DBs do not have the opportunity to witness Solars and Lunars outside of a wyld hunt. The majority of Dragonblooded are locked into aristocratic, virulently hierarchical and classist societies that both isolate them from interacting with other social classes and outsiders and diminish their empathy from them. For the average Dynastic Dragonblooded to give Solars or Lunars the benefit of the doubt requires a level of empathy and goodwill for the Other that they are simply <i>socialized against having</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:53:13-07:00","id":1404065,"title":"","content":"It would be accurate to call Immaculate Dragon Blooded deluded, but not really that they've deluded themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are?p=1404048#post1404048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't think on Sidereals most of the time. The 3e books ont he topic note that Sidereals basically are hidden agents of Heaven. The stuff about them in general in the exoteric stuff most folks get is that wise people come up now and again and give the Dragon-Blooded advice. Those in the know about htem usually see them as agents of Heaven who give input in the needs of Desitny, tend to give good advice, and like the Dragon-Blooded are spiritually enlightened enough to handle this stuff. &quot;Hidden equals&quot; is kind of the gist I think the Sidereals want to present themselves as in context of the Philosophy, but again, most folks don't even know who they are, and there are some who do know about htem who don't trust them but see them as anicllary to the Philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a lot of the time the first thing somebody will assume when they see a Sidereal is that they're an Exigent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T21:55:52-07:00","id":1404168,"title":"","content":"My play-group's take on it is that the &quot;Demon-possessed humans&quot; line is all the average person or even Dragon-Blooded needs to know. &quot;Anathema Bad&quot; is a simple message to convey and avoids a lot of the complexity involved. That being said any amount of actual research into it gets past the intro explanation and explains that they are exalts who are overwhelmed by their exaltations and are driven crazy / evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T12:23:58-07:00","id":1404957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1403917-do-the-dragon-blooded-truly-delude-themselves-the-solars-and-lunars-are?p=1403937#post1403937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fun thing to consider: because Dragon-Blooded Exaltations tend to occur before Celestial Exaltations do, and since they\u2019re mutually exclusive, anyone who Exalts as a Solar or Lunar by definition was passed over by the Dragons. The Sun and the Moon only choose mortals unsuited to leadership, making their wondrous powers of leadership a terrible curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of an observation an Earth Aspect of mine made after she ditched the realm (she was a peasant on the blessed isle, not a dynast), and started hanging out with a Solar in the Threshold:<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm starting to realize something: the Realm doesn't hate the Anathema because they're powerful. They hate the Anathema because they <i>shouldn't</i> be powerful. You spend your whole childhood waiting for the Dragons to grace you and then some random street punk gets to turn into a silver lion. Damn, I'd be kinda pissed too. Not enough to make a whole damn religion out of sheer spite, but hey. Can't blame 'em.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T20:04:41-07:00","id":1405116,"title":"","content":"One thing that I think about is the possibility that people in a state of anger or bitterness or grief can start to actively (if not quite intentionally) eliminate their sense of nuance regarding a subject; details that would be contrary to their emotional state become less apparent, while they can indeed start to see elements that reinforce and justify how they feel that aren't truly there.<br /> <br /> I look at the example of the Iron Flame clan among the Toumon, and the reference to how they're courting the Immaculate Philosophy, because they happen to have never accumulated much in the way of the usual tutelary ancestor ghosts and have been particularly subject to assault by alien gods (while also having an apparent economic base that I would read as putting them somewhere equivalent to a comfortable enough middle class existence to be isolated from other afflicted clans while also being stung by the lack of social or political prestige underlined by the absence of divine favour and any associated lesser contribution to the more prominent martial undertakings).<br /> <br /> We're notably not told how this is reconciled with the presence of Wake. I can hardly imagine that a Lunar being in their midst has gone unnoticed by the Immaculate missionaries, and even if some form of syncretism was tolerable the point is rendered moot with the pains she has gone to in order to not be regarded as a divinity. I would imagine that for a start, they would quietly sidestep the point that the immortal hero-aunt is an intolerable monster, but eventually they're going to have to bring it up and the Iron Flame are going to have to decide how to feel about that.<br /> <br /> I picture a scenario in which things come to a head at some kind of major social or political event past the point where more people have realised that a clan has widely adopted the Immaculate Philosophy, and word has been widely spread that this entails labelling Wake Anathema. That members of the Iron Flame might feel ganged up on as everybody else demands, in a mixture of tones of outrage and frustration and sorrow, how they can side with a people that would despise Wake so, after everything she's done for them. And in that moment I can see a loud voice shout back something to the effect of &quot;everything that she's done for <i>you</i>, you mean&quot;.<br /> <br /> And it's not really a thing that they've thought before, but in the heat of the moment and the need to defend and justify oneself and just plain being driven to win the argument, it boils up and starts to gather momentum. And everything that Wake actually has done for them, specifically, starts to fade from their attention, and they rile themselves up more with the idea that everything they ever suffered at the hands of gods shows a failure by Wake to protect them, which can build into a narrative of her complicity, which can ultimately end in a place that conflates her with the devils that did her harm. They fold in every instance of seeing Wake in battle, and feats that were once celebrated are now pointed to as indicators of her malefic nature. People double down as they feel more alienated and wronged, and they emphasize and embellish and conflate the details to feed a narrative that supports everything they're feeling, and it comes to a point where they declare that the Toumon have been deluding themselves to ever think that Wake was safe to be around, and it's only a matter of time before she turns on all of them (it's awfully convenient that she can attribute the loss of her own people to somebody else, isn't it?). Well, we're not going to be deluded any more; we're leaving before it's too late, and we're taking our property and our expertise that can establish us in some other more sensible commune with us. You can have your devil-warrior, and best hope that your fading ancestors can protect you if she ever turns those martial talents upon yourselves. <br /> <br /> Probably not a situation that entails the entire clan rising in violence against the Lunar specifically, but maybe a few young zealots (egged on in secret by some of the missionaries) make an attempt. Perhaps Wake tries to shield the Iron Flame from reprisals by the rest of the clans; it breaks her heart that one of them is rejecting her like this (and insinuations about her past might push her to the brink), but for the sake of the memory of better times and the friendship she recalls she's willing to allow them depart unmolested and not hold the actions of an eager few that didn't amount to much against them. Perhaps it proves that such restraint lies beyond her power, and the seceding clan is fallen upon by their fellows who are enraged beyond reason at the treachery and ingratitude and dishonour. Any who make it out despite that might find other stories of what Lunars can do that they can seize upon to recall Wake as having used twisted words to affect magnanimity while actually turning everybody else against them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, apart from indulging in this scenario having occurred to me as I imagined the Iron Flame's conversion playing out in similar terms to impulses for viewing other people that I've had to curb during some extreme periods, I can see this as a way that Dragon Blooded ideas about the nature of the other Exalted could have evolved that have a bit more going on for them than just making something up wholecloth and then committing to it deeply. That a narrative which emphasizes Celestial offences can cross over with many people technically not being well-acquainted with the mechanisms of their Exaltation &quot;people who almost literally acquired demon powers&quot;. It wouldn't have been helped by the fact that the period in which these narratives are developing is one in which most of the Solars are removed from sight while the Lunars are drawing deep from their scariest toybox. One might wonder if any Dragon Blooded who are starting to promote the rhetoric of being demon sorcerers are doing so while afflicted with that curse to literally wear down your capacity to feel anything other than terror that a Lunar is hunting you. Over time they just start to conflate the memory of the Solars with what is becoming more of an everyday reality, even if the powers of those Exalted diverged significantly at important points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T08:39:39-07:00","id":1405347,"title":"","content":"As for the role of the Sun and Moon in exalting Anathema, i'd imagine that the average orthodox theologian would try to dance around the question or subtly(but <i>never</i> directly) imply that the Sun and Moon are in fact amoral, capricious, or irresponsible. Regardless of the virtues and power of the Anathema, their might is ultimately inauspicious and corruptive and their connection to the Incarnae, legitimate or otherwise, has no bearing on their morality, because the Incarnae are not moral actors in the Immaculate doctrine. Much like how <i>The Ramayana</i>, a Vaishnavite Hindu text(meaning it places emphasis on Vishnu as the greatest of gods) subtly casts Lord Shiva and Brahma in a negative light for empowering the Rakshasa King Ravana. It never goes so far as to condemn them, but it certainly does not assign them any moral superiority over or even moral equivalency with Vishnu.<br /> <br /> The immaculate order and philosophy are largely a patchwork job to unite pre-Usurpation theology with the political goals of the Bronze Faction and the Realm, there are going to be flaws and weaknesses in the doctrine, but those have been planned around and believers are often socialized to ignore those weaknesses. The Immaculates have several well-constructed, and <i>technically true</i> arguments for hunting Anathema, and they reinforce this by imparting a values system to believers that categorically excludes and dehumanizes Anathema regardless of their behavior. In that values system, Anathema are dangerous because they ignore the Perfected Hierarchy from which the Dragon-Blooded derive authority, making their existence an <i>existential</i> threat against the Dragon-Blooded hegemony. For an ordinary Dragon-Blooded to consider showing mercy or empathy for Anathema requires them to act against what they perceive as their own best interests, which most are not inclined to do. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T13:41:45-07:00","id":1405402,"title":"","content":"<i>Sister Ivy frowned as she lowered the scroll her sifu had given her. &quot;So... The Anathema aren't demons,&quot; she said, chewing on her lower lip.<br /> <br /> &quot;That's right,&quot; her sifu said, dutifully taking the scroll and rolling it up. &quot;It is a story we tell the populace at large. Only those who show focus and dedication and piety, like yourself, can know the truth.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sifu, why?&quot; Ivy asked. &quot;Why do we tell the faithful and the other Dragon Bloods that the Anathema are demons?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Sifu frowned and sighed, rising to his feet. &quot;Walk with me, Ivy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Out of the archives, and in the sand garden of the temple, the sifu finally spoke again. &quot;When you tell the parable of the farmer, the hen, and the fox, that is not literally about an actual farmer, a hen, and a troublesome fox. Except when it is, I suppose.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, yes,&quot; Ivy said. &quot;But that's simplifying something to make it easier to understand. This... Is a lie.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;... Yes. It is,&quot; her sifu said. &quot;The exact nature of the Anathema is a secret teaching, and them being demons who stole the power of the Sun and Moon is a lie. But something that isn't a lie is what that power does to someone.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sifu?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Sun and Moon are great, Sister,&quot; her Sifu said as he approached a pond, producing a bag of seeds and tossing them to the ducks swimming merrily. &quot;Too great for a mortal to even comprehend. Even if through circumstance, a mortal is Exalted by the Sun or Moon, that is far greater power than any mortal can, or should, have.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;So when we teach that the Anathema will go mad-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That is NOT a lie,&quot; her Sifu said firmly. &quot;I have, in the past, engaged in more than a few Wyld Hunts. I've seen Anathema that do their best, that try to rein in the chaos of their Essence, that swear that they're different. Do you know how many I saw that didn't go mad and leave ruin and upheaval in their wake?&quot;<br /> <br /> There was a moment of silence before Ivy spoke. &quot;Is the answer 'None', Sifu?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Precisely. The Anathema are human, perhaps, but <b>more</b>. Do you recall your Exaltation, Ivy?&quot; the sifu said, tossing more seeds to the ducks.<br /> <br /> &quot;It was... Exhilarating, Sifu. I felt so much power, like I could do anything...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;From what we know, the passions of the Chosen of the Dragons are great and must be tempered. It is also true with the Anathema. And their ability to do more is even greater. Imagine someone with the impulses of you when you first Exalted... With the power you've heard and seen from the Anathema.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ivy didn't say anything, simply frowned. Finally, she broke the silence. &quot;I don't doubt that Anathema are dangerous, Sifu, But why do we tell the rest of Creation this story? Can't they know the truth?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Some can,&quot; her Sifu said. &quot;But for a grieving family, it may be easier to tell them that their child is already dead, and that it's a demon, rather than explain that their child is doomed to madness and to lose themselves.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ivy frowned, clenching her fists on her knees. &quot;... I don't know how I feel about this, Sifu.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Neither did I, when I first heard it. In time, I've seen this happen far too often. And when you're on a Hunt... Sometimes happiness is the greater good over technicalities.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another moment of silence before Ivy spoke up. &quot;I will... Think on this, Sifu.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 07-31-2020, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}